 "what_the_frozen_numbers_mean": [
  "'wells' for the development arms are logical per-pair charges, not plate wells",
  "the conventional search's 167,722 wells are the cost of reading every known query outcome once for each candidate batch; it is a data-access convention, not a recommended experimental design",
  "deployment wells (28 per line) are identical across arms; arms differ only in how they spend them",
  "the 10-program seed library has zero incremental wells and no compute; its cost is authoring effort, not measured",
  "development outcomes read for the distinguishing experiment were also inside the training of the frozen bench's folds (AUDIT_ACCESS.json): the wells charged measure the pairs revealed after commitment, not the query information the loop used"
 ]
